{"id": "1.2-00037", "case_id": "opencores_i2c_master_v1", "parent_id": null, "source": "opencores/communication_controller_i2c_controller_core", "record_protocol": null, "panels": {"stored": "<h2>Agent task and scoring</h2><div class='card'><table><tbody><tr><th style='width:175px'>Input task</th><td class='path'>Project specification, interfaces, and permitted public assets</td></tr><tr><th style='width:175px'>Agent context</th><td class='path'>Direct agent workspace: <a href='#task=1.2&amp;case=1.2-00037&amp;file_q=public%2F'>public/</a> (6 files)</td></tr><tr><th style='width:175px'>Expected output</th><td class='path'>Required RTL: rtl/verilog/i2c_master_bit_ctrl.v, rtl/verilog/i2c_master_byte_ctrl.v, rtl/verilog/i2c_master_top.v. <a href='#task=1.2&amp;case=1.2-00037&amp;file=public%2Foutput_contract.json'>Open full output contract</a></td></tr><tr><th style='width:175px'>Hidden reference</th><td class='path'>3 RTL files under private/reference/; <a href='#task=1.2&amp;case=1.2-00037&amp;file=private%2Freference%2Frtl%2Fverilog%2Fi2c_master_bit_ctrl.v'>open first reference file</a></td></tr><tr><th style='width:175px'>Private score</th><td class='path'>Passed verification testpoints divided by total testpoints, using testbenches or formal verification<br><strong>4 verification testpoints:</strong> registers, transactions, clock_stretch, arbitration. <a href='#task=1.2&amp;case=1.2-00037&amp;file=private%2Fscoring.json'>Open private scoring contract</a></td></tr></tbody></table></div><h2>Case-stored agent instruction</h2><div class='card'><p class='muted'>These are case-stored instructions. A launcher may add framing or execution limits; its saved trajectory is the exact runtime record.</p><details><summary>public/instruction.md · <a href='#task=1.2&amp;case=1.2-00037&amp;file=public%2Finstruction.md'>Open raw</a></summary><pre># Implement the Wishbone I2C master project\nRead the original PDF, the output contract and the declaration-only interfaces.\nImplement i2c_master_top, i2c_master_byte_ctrl and i2c_master_bit_ctrl in their\nrequired paths. Headers are preprocessed privately to freeze the original default\nconfiguration; provide synthesizable modules without includes or simulation delays.\n\nClarifications for this pinned release:\n- Top wb_rst_i is active-high synchronous. arst_i has configurable active level\n  ARST_LVL (default 0, active-low asynchronous). Child nReset is active-low\n  asynchronous and rst active-high synchronous. Reset initializes released bus\n  lines; pad_o outputs are always zero, pad_oen=1 means release/open-drain high.\n- Register addresses 0/1 prescaler low/high (reset FFFF), 2 control (reset zero),\n  3 transmit write / receive read, 4 command write / status read. Address 5 reads\n  the stored transmit byte, 6 reads the command register, 7 returns zero. Read\n  data registers every clock. Wishbone ACK alternates while cyc/stb are held;\n  hold writes for two rising edges because write acceptance uses old ACK.\n- Control bit 7 enables the engine, bit 6 enables IRQ. Other control bits are\n  stored/read. Command writes are ignored while disabled. Command bits are\n  START[7], STOP[6], READ[5], WRITE[4], ACK-to-send[3] (1=NACK), IACK[0].\n  Bits 7:4 clear on done/arbitration loss, bits 2:1 clear, IACK self-clears.\n  Bit 3 persists. Use only valid commands, clearing enable only when idle.\n- Status: RXACK[7] (1=NACK), bus-busy[6], arbitration-lost[5], zeros[4:2],\n  transfer-in-progress[1], interrupt-flag[0]. Completion/arbitration sets sticky\n  flag; command IACK clears it. IRQ is the registered flag AND control[6].\n- Serial transfers are 8 bits MSB first plus ACK, with START, repeated START,\n  STOP, slave clock stretching and bus arbitration. Prescaler gives approximately\n  SCL = wb_clk/(5*(prescaler+1)); this release synchronizes and filters SCL/SDA.\n  Losing arbitration releases both lines and clears the command. Busy tracks\n  observed START/STOP. A transmitted one observed as zero loses arbitration.\n- Byte controller starts a transfer on read or write, optionally emits START,\n  shifts eight bits and receives/sends ACK, optionally STOP, then pulses cmd_ack.\n  ack_out contains received ACK and dout the received/shifted byte. Hold command\n  inputs until completion, then clear them before requesting another operation.\n- Bit-controller 4-bit commands: NOP=0, START=1, STOP=2, READ=4, WRITE=8.\n  A command emits its bus waveform and pulses cmd_ack. din selects transmitted\n  data; dout samples SDA. Handshake/timing follows the byte controller and PDF;\n  internal state encodings and pipeline organization need not copy the reference.\n\nPrivate points check register behavior, full slave memory transactions with\nrepeated START and ACK/NACK, clock stretching, and arbitration loss. The finite\ntests are not exhaustive formal equivalence. Public checks give compilation only.\n\nImplement every required path in output_contract.json. Declaration-only ports\nare in interfaces/modules.v. No initial/final, delays, simulation system tasks,\nforce/release or external includes are permitted. Only declared RTL is collected.\nMissing files, forbidden constructs or failed top compilation score zero. Each\nprivate point has equal weight and requires all of its checks to pass. Use\nterminal/file_editor, iverilog, vvp and Python iteratively; finish by saving RTL.\nRun `python3 checks/check.py` for public compilation feedback.\n</pre></details></div>"}, "files": [{"name": "case.json", "url": "assets/59a8b36e3688c45d92d3f8f5fc3778c66c122c483ff848355117ab092a4a8024.txt", "size": 31994, "binary": false, "section": "Other: case.json"}, {"name": "environment/runtime.json", "url": "assets/771e58998dfa59d19bd4591ce49673fcbadd56239829b74d2a9c5869aef77295.txt", "size": 4693, "binary": false, "section": "Other: environment"}, {"name": "private/original_reference/rtl/verilog/i2c_master_bit_ctrl.v", "url": "assets/1f9e5988d047897d5322a06095e209750d21712d2d2c6936703cb8fc802ca